{"term":"corridor","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4a6daf54e246b6ac7b","definition":"A narrow hall or passage with rooms leading off it, as in a building or in a railway carriage.","example":"There is an hour or two, after the passengers have embarked, which is disquieting and fussy.[…]Stewards, carrying cabin trunks, swarm in the corridors. Passengers wander restlessly about or hurry, with futile energy, from place to place.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air corridor","boom corridor","corridor care","corridor discussion","corridor disease","corridored","corridorless","corridorlike","corridor of uncertainty","corridor shooter","corridors of power","corridor train","corridor warrior","Danubian corridor","economic corridor","ghost corridor","green corridor","humanitarian corridor","M62 corridor","Mormon corridor","non-corridor","noncorridor","Northeast Corridor","Suwalki corridor","utilidor","wildlife corridor"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corridor#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a2c82b4535b90a8a0b","definition":"A restricted tract of land that allows passage between two places.","example":"In addition, there are two up and two down korridorzug ^([sic]) [Korridorzüge] of the O.B.B. which run through from Innsbruck to Reutte via the Mittenwald line, but which are \"sealed\" between Scharnitz through Garmisch-Partenkirchen as far as Ehrwald, carrying passengers only from Austria to Austria; the korridor thus refers to the corridor through Germany and not through the train.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air corridor","boom corridor","corridor care","corridor discussion","corridor disease","corridored","corridorless","corridorlike","corridor of uncertainty","corridor shooter","corridors of power","corridor train","corr